The English translation in this directory is dedicated to the public domain
under CC0 1.0 Universal.

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

WHAT THIS COVERS

Everything in translation/en/ — the new English rendering of Francesco
Colonna's Hypnerotomachia Poliphili (Venice: Aldus Manutius, 1499), chapters
XVII to XXXVIII and the epitaphs, being the roughly 59% of the book that
Robert Dallington's 1592 English never reached.

It also covers that English wherever else it appears in this project: in
research/translation.html, and in the passages quoted inside the application.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

The Italian in translation/source/ is not ours to license. It is the 1499
original, public domain by age, transcribed by contributors to Italian
Wikisource from the MIT Press facsimile.

WHY CC0

There is no freely reusable English for this part of the book. Dallington stops
at facsimile page 193 of 467, and every complete English translation since is
under copyright. A licence with conditions — even attribution — would keep this
text out of Wikisource, out of future critical editions, and out of the hands of
the scholars most likely to want it. CC0 removes every obstacle to that reuse.

CITATION IS REQUESTED, NOT REQUIRED

If you use this, we would like to be cited, and it costs you nothing to do so.
But it is a request between people, not a condition of the licence, and nothing
here obliges you to honour it.

The translation is a working draft. Pages marked "drafted" rather than
"verified" still carry readings we have flagged as uncertain against the
facsimile. Check translation/manifest.json for the status of any page before
relying on it.
